ee what looks like an  LAPD officer bringing him some other guy  who comes up looks at the suspect and  nod I'm going to assume that this is a  witness of the crime who they're  bringing in to identify the criminal if  that was the case then it seems like  they did get the right guy because after  that the guards convened and seemed to  be like making a plan to escort the  suspect out of this train station and as  soon as that happens the train gets  moving  before that though they made one last  announcement on the intercom and said  that the train ahead of us in Universal  City was successfully taken off the  track and we could get underway and  that's the part that I hated most about  the way that this was handled there are  windows on the train everyone saw what  just went on we aren't stupid there's no  reason to lie and patronize your  customers dude we got to Universal City  and there are a couple people who got on  the train at that point and I tried  asking if anything had gone down at that  stop but unfortunately they didn't speak  English so I wasn't able to get any more  information I still have no idea how  that guy in the brown shirt knew that  the grey shirt guy was the one that they  were looking for based on such a generic  description he may have very well saved  us though so props to that guy the rest  of my trip to Chicago is safe exactly  one year after being eliminated on the  day that Back to the Future 2  prophesized that we would become  champions I was on the way home to the  finale of the NLCS  the next day Kyle Hendricks outdueled  clayton kershaw for the pennant and then  11  well technically 12 days later the  drought came to an end and the ghosts of  harry carey could finally rest in peace  speaking of the ghosts of harry carey  join me next time on true.you as i jump  back to five years ago when the ghost of  harry caray appeared in our group  photograph not clickbait i actually have  proof so if you want to hear about that  or if you